---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ToolShell from '../components/ToolShell.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import RelatedTools from '../components/RelatedTools.astro';
---

<Layout title="Convert subtitles to SRT online" description="Convert VTT, ASS, SSA, SAMI, MicroDVD, or MPL2 subtitles to SRT online. Preview changes before download. Files stay on your device.">
  <h1>Convert subtitles to SRT</h1>
  <p class="lede">Convert VTT, ASS, SSA, SAMI, SUB, or MPL2 files to SRT for players, editors, and uploads.</p>

  <ToolShell columns={['#', 'Start', 'End', 'Text']} />

  <section class="help">
    <h2>How to convert a subtitle file to SRT</h2>
    <p>Upload a file, check the cue preview, then download the SRT. Cue times and dialogue stay in place, and the converter adds clean SRT numbering.</p>
    <h2>Supported formats</h2>
    <p>Convert WebVTT, ASS, SSA, SAMI, MicroDVD, and MPL2. MicroDVD files use video frames, so select the video's frame rate when the file does not include one.</p>
    <h2>What SRT keeps</h2>
    <p>SRT keeps cue times, text, and basic bold, italic, or underline tags. Positions, karaoke timing, and format-specific styles have no SRT equivalent. The preview lists anything the conversion drops.</p>
    <pre><code>Input: 00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.000
Output: 00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:04,000</code></pre>
    <h2>When the output looks wrong</h2>
    <p>Try another source encoding if letters are garbled. Choose the correct frame rate for MicroDVD. SUP/PGS and VobSub are image subtitles, so they need OCR before this text converter can read them.</p>
    <p>Run the result through the <a href="/subtitle-validator">SRT validator</a>, then <a href="/srt-cleaner">clean the subtitle text</a> if needed.</p>
  </section>

  <Faq title="SRT converter FAQ" items={[
    { question: 'Can I convert VTT to SRT?', answer: 'Yes. Upload a WebVTT file and download an SRT with the same cue times and dialogue.' },
    { question: 'Can I convert ASS to SRT?', answer: 'Yes. ASS and SSA dialogue converts to SRT. Positions, karaoke timing, and some styling are listed as dropped.' },
    { question: 'Why does my converted SRT look wrong?', answer: 'Try a different source encoding or choose the correct frame rate for MicroDVD. Image subtitles need OCR before conversion.' },
  ]} />

  <RelatedTools tools={[
    { href: '/subtitle-validator', label: 'Validate the SRT', description: 'Find bad timestamps and overlap or empty-cue problems.' },
    { href: '/srt-cleaner', label: 'Clean the subtitles', description: 'Remove tags, music notes, labels, or duplicate cues.' },
    { href: '/utf-8-converter', label: 'Fix garbled text', description: 'Read an old encoding and save the file as UTF-8.' },
    { href: '/subtitle-shifter', label: 'Fix subtitle timing', description: 'Move every cue earlier or later by one offset.' },
  ]} />
</Layout>

<script>
  import { mountConverter } from '../components/converter.ts';
  mountConverter('srt');
</script>

<style>
  :global(.tool td:nth-child(-n + 3)) { white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  :global(.tool td:last-child) { width: 100%; }
</style>
